{"number": 89, "text": "                Exercises\n\n\n        41.1\n                Divide the exclamations and warnings  on the\n                opposite page into these groups:\n                a) those that you could use to your boss or teacher\n                b) those that you could use only to close friends\n        41.2\n                Choose  the best response from those in the box to\n                fit each of these dialogues.\n\n                 Come  offit!  Lightenup!   Steadyon!    Mind out!\n                 Holdon!    Comeon!    Spititout!   Keep it up!\n\n                1    Nicholas       sorry, | just haven’t had time to finish my essay. It’s taken me ages to get hold\n                                of the books | needed for it.\n                     Teacher                    There are plenty of copies in the library. And you could have told\n                                me  sooner if you had really been having problems.\n                2 ~  Amelia     Can | speak to your sister, please?\n                    “Matt                       I'll just go and see if she’s home yet.\n                     Elliot     What’s the matter with you?\n                     Millie     There’s something I’ve got to tell you but, well, | don’t know where to begin.\n                     Elliot                     | haven’t got all day.\n                4    Bella       I’m never going to get all this work done. | hate my job.\n                     Naomi                       It won’t take long if you hurry up a bit.\n                     Anna        Look at the picture on the side of that lorry!\n                     Tom                        You’re going to hit the car in front of you!\n                6    Aisha      That was a stupid thing to do. You’re fired!\n                     Harvey                     You know  I’m one of your best workers.\n                7 ~~ Archie      Now I’ve been in the office for a month, I’d like to know if you are pleased with my\n                                 work. How am | doing?\n                     Rob        Very well!                You’ll soon be getting a promotion.\n                Answer  the following questions.\n        41.3\n                 1 Which exclamation on the opposite page is connected with the idea of shooting a gun?\n                 2 Which exclamation is connected with the idea of forcing out the liquid in your mouth?\n                                                                   i                  imately the same\n                              lamations  from the box below into pairs that have approxima\n        41.4\n                 meaning “What  is the basic meaning for each pair? Describe a situation when each pair of\n                 expressions might be used.\n                  Watch out!     Hold on!    Mind out!    Hurry up!    Go on!    Hang on!\n\n\n                                                               English Phrasal Verbs in Use Intermediate   87", "char_count": 2936, "mean_conf": 92.33, "word_count": 359, "words": [{"text": "41.1", "x0": 163, "y0": 306, "x1": 269, "y1": 349, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "41.2", "x0": 165, "y0": 590, "x1": 271, "y1": 632, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "41.3", "x0": 178, "y0": 2504, "x1": 283, "y1": 2543, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "41.4", "x0": 180, "y0": 2727, "x1": 286, "y1": 2766, "conf": 94, "bold": false}, {"text": "Exercises", "x0": 343, "y0": 93, "x1": 709, "y1": 163, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Divide", "x0": 343, "y0": 308, "x1": 474, "y1": 345, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "the", "x0": 486, "y0": 310, "x1": 556, "y1": 346, "conf": 92, "bold": true}, {"text": "exclamations", "x0": 570, "y0": 313, "x1": 851, "y1": 352, "conf": 92, "bold": false}, {"text": "and", "x0": 864, "y0": 320, "x1": 940, "y1": 354, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "warnings", "x0": 955, "y0": 321, "x1": 1146, "y1": 367, "conf": 94, "bold": false}, {"text": "on", 